    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the clear headliner. Boasting an elite 87.14 efficiency score, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Mikolas (4.71 xERA), but his real value is magnified by the \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor, which projectable bumps his steal efficiency by 4%. Joining him in the elite tier is **Gabriel Moreno** (70.58), whose profile is buoyed by a strong 0.381 xwOBA and a favorable matchup in the #3 hole. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (69.70) remains a lock despite facing a lefty; his raw power and elite xwOBA (0.423) provide the necessary floor to ignore traditional platoon splits, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Seiya Suzuki**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 47.00 score. While **Seiya Suzuki** offers a reliable presence in the #2 hole, he was edged out by the superior matchup context for **Austin Riley** (71.27) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13). **Austin Riley** is particularly fascinating today, as a high park factor and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus on the mound significantly boost his outlook despite his presence in the bottom third of the lineup. Conversely, we must monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** (48.26); currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" his score is suppressed by a brutal matchup against the arm of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez (2.82 xERA). Owners should also take note of **Josh Naylor** (49.91), who is effectively playing for his spot today against the high-skill arm of deGrom, where his projected efficiency sits dangerously close to the 40.0 bench threshold. Proceed with caution on **Jose Caballero** if the official lineup drops him further down the order, as that could necessitate a pivot to **Seiya Suzuki** to preserve our plate appearance caps.",
